{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UnitalGroebnerBasesChapter.SPolynomial","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UnitalGroebnerBasesChapter.SPolynomial","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.SPolynomial.scalar₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.SPolynomial.scalar₂","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/s-polynomial.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The cancellation scalar for the second element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.SPolynomial.scalar₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.SPolynomial.scalar₁","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/s-polynomial.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The cancellation scalar for the first element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.SPolynomial.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.SPolynomial.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/s-polynomial.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.SPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.GrobnerShirshov.ContentBlock.SPolynomial","kind":"structure","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/s-polynomial.lean#L26-L42","doc":"An **S-polynomial** combination of two elements `f₁, f₂` of the free\nalgebra `k⟨G⟩` with cancellation scalars `a₁, a₂`. This mirrors the\n`λ·u·f·v − λ'·u'·f'·v'` construction of the paper once the\nadmissible multiples have been absorbed into `f₁, f₂`.\n\n**`leadingTermsAgree : Prop` removed 2026-09-07. Its docstring called it \"a flag\nrecording that the construction is applicable\" — and typed with the\n*universe* `Prop` it recorded nothing, since an instance chose the\nproposition. Neither read nor constructed. The real condition\n`λ·LT(u·LT(f)·v) = λ'·LT(u'·LT(f')·v')` needs the elements and the\nleading-term map, which this manifest structure does not carry.** ","signatureChunk":0}]}